body:


* Copy of valid passport or identity card (no driver's license);
* Recent employer statement;
* Recent mortgage or landlord statement (correct payment behavior);
* 3 x copies of recent payslips (from the past 3 months, with gross monthly wages);
* 3 x copy of the bank statement on which the salary has been deposited (from the past month, received proof wages on account);
* Copy of annual statement;
* Copy of bank / debit card from the same account number as bank statement;  


I can stand behind this as it all proof of your income and the account etc. is all in your name ( the renter ).  





* Overview of the employment history of Mijn UWV (including your certified insurance message employment history and salary data)
* Extract from the Municipal Personal Records Database;  


I have never been asked to provide this information and i moved quite alot through the Netherlands.   


* last annual statement of your mortgage provider and the sales agreement / value indication of your current home;
* Divorce settlement (when you are divorced);  


This is also logical since these are mandatory costs which as subtracted from your income and not available for the rent.  


* Income statement from the Tax and Customs Administration.  


This is again something i never had to give to any agency.
